(quine completion (eval (do (quine prompt "Find the sum of 1+2+...+100, then compute the average. Use (think \"...\" code...) for reasoning. If a thought was wrong, (rethink \"...\" code...) corrects it. After every rethink, your trailing expression must be '(!extend completion) — this prunes rethought expressions from the context, then calls !llm-self. Do not use reopen; use !extend. think, rethink, !extend are built-in macros.") (think "The sum 1+2+...+n = n*(n+1). So 100*101 = 10100." (def total (* 100 101)))